<title>ESTONIA: HOIU SHAREHOLDERS APPROVE PROPOSALS.</title>
<headline>HOIU SHAREHOLDERS APPROVE PROPOSALS.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hoiupank shareholders have approved a profit distribution plan and proposed changes in the board.</p>
<p>Under the profit distribution plan approved at a shareholder meeting on Saturday, the bank will cover the losses of previous years with 20.7 million kroons and transfer 47.26 million kroons to the general reserve.</p>
<p>Hoiupank made a 1996 net profit of 67.96 million kroons.</p>
<p>Hoiupank shareholders voted Sparbanken Sverige executive vice-president Lars-Olof Odlund as a new board member.</p>
<p>Swedish Sparbanken acquired 12.5 percent of Hoiupank shares last December from Hansapank .</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
